= V1 category migration =

V1 uses 162 category names and zero authored <code>Category:</code> pages. The exact set and every member are preserved in <code>archive-v1/categories/index.json</code> and <code>archive-v1/categories/members/</code>.

V2 does '''not''' delete that history and does '''not''' blindly recreate all 162 labels. It asks what semantic job each category was doing and moves that job to the correct MediaWiki/SMW primitive.

== Functional refactor ==

{| class="wikitable"
! V1 category function !! Representative V1 categories !! V2 representation
|-
| Knowledge domain / subject || Systems Science, Systems Theory, Network Science, Cybernetics, Information Theory, Biology, Philosophy, Philosophy of Science, Data Science, Computational Methods, Blockchain, Metaphysics || <code>Domain</code> property + intentional domain/category/portal when useful. Normalize naming; do not duplicate the same domain under several labels.
|-
| Entity / page type || Concepts, Ideas, Implementations, Projects, Protocols, Datasets, People, Events, Publications, Constructs, Topics || <code>Entity type</code> semantic dimension. Human category only when it provides a useful browse surface.
|-
| Epistemic status || Hypothetical, Emerging, Established, Verified, Axiomatic and the parallel “... Claims” variants || <code>Epistemic status</code> / evidence model. Do not maintain a second epistemic ontology purely as categories.
|-
| BITwiki system role || BITwiki Front Matter, Constitutional, Governance, Ontology, Schema Matter, Templates, Index/Indexes, Operational, Architecture, Technical Guide/Reference/Specification || <code>BITwiki:</code> namespace + a small curated meta category set such as BITwiki foundations, governance, architecture, templates, Navigation and Provenance.
|-
| Book Matter / reusable section || Applications, Definition Fragments, Evidence Summary Fragments, Methodology Fragments, Protocol Fragments, Topic Sections, Transcludable Content, Main Page Sections || Book Matter headings/subpages/transclusion. Category only when there is a genuine collection to browse.
|-
| Workflow / provenance / migration || Phase 1, Breaking Changes, Migrated Content, Revision - Coraline Integration, Hyperion Workspace, BITwiki Agents, Transparency, Wikipedia Source || Revision/source/provenance/workflow metadata. Preserve historical attribution without making temporary workflow state a permanent subject taxonomy.
|-
| Validation / error state || Infobox ... missing ..., Pages with script errors, Pages with broken file links, Property type error, Template Error, Constraint violation || Generated validation categories or Special-page reports. Treat as operational diagnostics, not knowledge ontology.
|-
| Imported/system vocabulary || Imported vocabulary, SMW Properties, SMW Property Definitions, SMW Templates || SMW/import configuration and provenance. Preserve imported vocabulary separately from BITwiki-native ontology.
|-
| Placeholder / malformed residue || <code>...</code>, <code>BITwiki ...</code>, <code>Name</code> || Archive exact membership, repair originating source, then retire from V2 taxonomy.
|}

Every V1 category remains individually inspectable in the archive. The table above is a refactor of '''function''', not a claim that every member of a broad category family is semantically identical.

== Canonical V2 category rules ==

# A category must have an intentional browse/index purpose.
# A created V2 Category page should explain what belongs there and, where useful, what does not.
# Category hierarchy is a navigation graph, not the ontology.
# Domain may be represented both semantically and as a human category when that improves browsing; the semantic <code>Domain</code> value remains authoritative for machine queries.
# Entity type, epistemic status, confidence, provenance and workflow state should not be duplicated into category trees merely because V1 did so.
# Maintenance/error categories may exist when generated by templates/extensions, but they are operational outputs and should not be presented as knowledge domains.
# Book Matter is content anatomy, not taxonomy.

== Current V2 category surface ==
V2 intentionally creates real Category pages, unlike V1. The initial public set includes:

=== Knowledge domains ===
Systems science, Science, Biology, Mathematics, Philosophy, Technology, Electronics, Energy, Engineering, Chemistry, Physics and Medicine under [[:Category:Knowledge domains]].

=== Project/system navigation ===
[[:Category:BITwiki meta]], [[:Category:BITwiki foundations]], [[:Category:BITwiki governance]], [[:Category:BITwiki architecture]], [[:Category:BITwiki templates]], [[:Category:Navigation]], [[:Category:Provenance]], [[:Category:Epistemics]], [[:Category:Portals]] and [[:Category:Domain exemplars]].

This is a floor. Additional categories are introduced from real V2 content needs, not by copying the entire V1 label set.

== Source preservation ==
For any disputed migration decision, inspect:
<pre>
archive-v1/categories/index.json
archive-v1/categories/members/<category>.json
archive-v1/pages/Main/Category List.mediawiki
archive-v1/pages/Main/CATEGORY ARCHITECTURE.mediawiki
relevant page revision history
</pre>

`Category List` is particularly useful because it reveals the intended dimensions explicitly: domain, entity type, BITwiki system role and epistemic tier. `CATEGORY ARCHITECTURE` adds temporal, attribution and workflow dimensions. V2 preserves these dimensions while separating their implementations.

